# Unit tests

- **Runner:** JUnit 5 (`org.junit.jupiter`). Use **Arrange / Act / Assert** comments in non-trivial tests.
- **Pure logic:** prefer tests that do not need HAL — package-visible helpers, small util/math types, command input mapping, drive kinematics/optimization helpers. No CAN, no full robot graph.
- **HAL / vendor sim:** `@ExtendWith(WpilibSimulationExtension.class)` when tests touch WPILib sim or vendor sim (joysticks, Spark, CTRE). Use isolated CAN IDs; close module/hardware handles in `@AfterEach` when tests construct real devices.
- **Do not** instantiate `Robot` or a full drivetrain subsystem graph in unit tests unless you add a dedicated fixture — extract testable logic instead (see `testsupport/` for shared sim setup).
- After changes, run `./gradlew test` (Java 17 toolchain from `build.gradle`).
